::Q046::[markdown]The **Imperfect (active, middle, passive)** forms are based on which Principal Part?:{
	~%-100%5th#Incorrect. **Imperfect (active, middle, passive)** forms are based on the **1st Principal Part**, not the 5th.
	~%100%1st#Correct: **Imperfect (active, middle, passive)** forms are based on the **1st Principal Part**.
	~%-100%3rd#Incorrect. **Imperfect (active, middle, passive)** forms are based on the **1st Principal Part**, not the 3rd.
	~%-100%6th#Incorrect. **Imperfect (active, middle, passive)** forms are based on the **1st Principal Part**, not the 6th.
	~%-100%2nd#Incorrect. **Imperfect (active, middle, passive)** forms are based on the **1st Principal Part**, not the 2nd.
	~%-100%4th#Incorrect. **Imperfect (active, middle, passive)** forms are based on the **1st Principal Part**, not the 4th.
}


::Q047::[markdown]I will wish:{
	~%-100%βούλομαι#Incorrect. **βούλομαι** is Principal Part 1 of **βούλομαι** “I want” (Chapter 11).
	~%100%ἐθελήσω#Correct: **ἐθελήσω** is Principal Part 2 of **ἐθέλω** “I will wish” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%ἕμεινα#Incorrect. **ἕμεινα** is Principal Part 3 of **μένω** “I remained” (Chapter 10).
	~%-100%πεπολίτευμαι#Incorrect. **πεπολίτευμαι** is Principal Part 5 of **πολῑτεύω** “I have been governed” (Chapter 6).
	~%-100%βεβούλημαι#Incorrect. **βεβούλημαι** is Principal Part 5 of **βούλομαι** “I have wanted” (Chapter 11).
	~%-100%ἐφυλάχθην#Incorrect. **ἐφυλάχθην** is Principal Part 6 of **φυλάττω** “I was guarded” (Chapter 3).
	~%-100%κελεύσω#Incorrect. **κελεύσω** is Principal Part 2 of **κελεύω** “I will command” (Chapter 2).
	~%-100%ἀκούω#Incorrect. **ἀκούω** is Principal Part 1 of **ἀκούω** “I hear” (Chapter 11).
}


::Q048::[markdown]I have wished:{
	~%-100%πεπαίδευκα#Incorrect. **πεπαίδευκα** is Principal Part 4 of **παιδεύω** “I have educated” (Chapter 2).
	~%-100%βάλλω#Incorrect. **βάλλω** is Principal Part 1 of **βάλλω** “I throw” (Chapter 11).
	~%-100%τάξω#Incorrect. **τάξω** is Principal Part 2 of **τάττω** “I will draw up (in battle)” (Chapter 4).
	~%100%ἠθέληκα#Correct: **ἠθέληκα** is Principal Part 4 of **ἐθέλω** “I have wished” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%ἤρχθην#Incorrect. **ἤρχθην** is Principal Part 6 of **ἄρχω** “I was ruled” (Chapter 5).
	~%-100%ἀξιώσω#Incorrect. **ἀξιώσω** is Principal Part 2 of **ἀξιόω** “I will think worthy of” (Chapter 10).
	~%-100%ἔπεμψα#Incorrect. **ἔπεμψα** is Principal Part 3 of **πέμπω** “I sent” (Chapter 2).
	~%-100%ἐθέλω#Incorrect. **ἐθέλω** is Principal Part 1 of **ἐθέλω** “I am willing” (Chapter 4).
}


::Q049::[markdown]ἐτύθην:{
	~%-100%I was stolen#Incorrect. **ἐκλάπην** is Principal Part 6 of **κλέπτω** “I was stolen” (Chapter 7).
	~%-100%I draw up (in battle)#Incorrect. **τάττω** is Principal Part 1 of **τάττω** “I draw up (in battle)” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%I have been left behind#Incorrect. **λέλειμμαι** is Principal Part 5 of **λείπω** “I have been left behind” (Chapter 7).
	~%-100%I was expected#Incorrect. **ἠξιώθην** is Principal Part 6 of **ἀξιόω** “I was expected” (Chapter 10).
	~%-100%I have been saved#Incorrect. **σέσωσμαι** is Principal Part 5 of **σῴζω** “I have been saved” (Chapter 7).
	~%100%I was sacrificed#Correct: **ἐτύθην** is Principal Part 6 of **θύω** “I was sacrificed” (Chapter 3).
	~%-100%I have been made clear#Incorrect. **δεδήλωμαι** is Principal Part 5 of **δηλόω** “I have been made clear” (Chapter 10).
	~%-100%I will stay#Incorrect. **μενῶ** is Principal Part 2 of **μένω** “I will stay” (Chapter 10).
}


::Q050::[markdown]The **4th Principal Part** is the::{
	~%-100%Aorist, Passive, Indicative, 1st person, Singular#Incorrect. The 4th Principal Part is **Perfect, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular**, not “Aorist, Passive, Indicative, 1st person, Singular”.
	~%-100%Aorist, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular#Incorrect. The 4th Principal Part is **Perfect, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular**, not “Aorist, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular”.
	~%-100%Present, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular#Incorrect. The 4th Principal Part is **Perfect, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular**, not “Present, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular”.
	~%-100%Perfect, Middle/Passive, Indicative, 1st person, Singular#Incorrect. The 4th Principal Part is **Perfect, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular**, not “Perfect, Middle/Passive, Indicative, 1st person, Singular”.
	~%-100%Future, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular#Incorrect. The 4th Principal Part is **Perfect, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular**, not “Future, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular”.
	~%100%Perfect, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular#Correct: the 4th Principal Part is **Perfect, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular**.
}


